                    {
                        "sense_id": "f5158185-9a89-3c0e-90be-b9b5f64cf08b",
                        "entry_id": "db595710-e827-375c-b7be-75d2297390a9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Selfie pris pendant l’administration d’un vaccin, généralement dans le but de promouvoir la vaccination."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Anglicism",
                            "neologism"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "670d2cc7-6ad8-4335-b55d-c0aa9864353b",
                                "sense_id": "f5158185-9a89-3c0e-90be-b9b5f64cf08b",
                                "text": "La pandémie de Covid-19 et le confinement auront été grands pourvoyeurs de néologismes. Et l’an 2021 a déjà vu naître son premier : vaxxie, contraction des mots « vaccin » et « selfie », en référence aux photos que les internautes partagent sur les réseaux sociaux après avoir reçu leur première injection."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0746fce7-67dc-45c3-b3e6-ac66ec48be94",
                                "sense_id": "f5158185-9a89-3c0e-90be-b9b5f64cf08b",
                                "text": "Manche retroussée, sourire aux lèvres, de nombreux anonymes ont à leur tour posté, avec une grande fierté, leur vaxxie sur les réseaux."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "017a00e2-fbc2-4270-b6d3-885dbb57ed85",
                        "source_entry_id": "db595710-e827-375c-b7be-75d2297390a9",
                        "source_sense_id": "f5158185-9a89-3c0e-90be-b9b5f64cf08b",
                        "target_lang_word": "vaxxie",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "vaxxie",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "60305932-b285-337b-a70a-7c24b173b564",
                                        "entry_id": "5914ec53-41cd-3762-a292-ea0a542bac5a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A photograph (especially a selfie) of a person receiving a vaccine, often shared on social media."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "neologism",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ac6f7f60-d4fc-47ee-987e-08aa6f5f038a",
                                                "sense_id": "60305932-b285-337b-a70a-7c24b173b564",
                                                "text": "Perhaps you’ve seen your first “vaxxies” — naturally, photos that people take of themselves getting a coronavirus vaccine and then post on social media. The country has already distributed over one million doses to health care workers, but who’s next?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d291d8f-9d21-4499-b5dd-511ec4269351",
                                                "sense_id": "60305932-b285-337b-a70a-7c24b173b564",
                                                "text": "Posting a ‘vaxxie’ (rarely a true a selfie, for logistical reasons) is becoming the unexpected social media trend of 2021, and led by a just as unexpected band of influencers. […] Inevitably, there will be some who deem vaxxies to be as smug, performative and fatuous as all other social media crazes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3957ab6e-5426-45e9-9592-7ffaf88bebcb",
                                                "sense_id": "60305932-b285-337b-a70a-7c24b173b564",
                                                "text": "As governments and health officials continue to flip-flop on vaccine age requirements, and anti-vaxxers spread falsehoods through social media and protests, the vaxxie might just be a powerful line of defence against vaccine hesitancy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "vaxxie",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6c8f56f1-f1ed-3668-acfd-356f70659da3",
                                        "entry_id": "d7fc51b6-0bca-33d9-b837-bc0cdbea0406",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who has received the COVID-19 vaccine."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "neologism",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "856db863-7a72-4400-84cd-78f52f35ce81",
                                                "sense_id": "6c8f56f1-f1ed-3668-acfd-356f70659da3",
                                                "text": "Vaxxie, Vaxxie, heart attacksie, Takes his tests and wears his maskies, Still got Covid, every strain, Got spike proteins in his brain"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
